; ONKEYUP/ONRELEASE: release mirrors of ONKEY/ONCLICK (see
; examples/onkey_onclick.logo) -- same background-invocation shape,
; just firing on key/button RELEASE instead of press. Useful for
; things like "stop moving when the arrow key is let go," which ONKEY
; alone can't express on its own. Only makes sense from the actual
; app: the headless test driver has no entry box/canvas to ever
; generate a real key/button-release event from.

TO KEYDOWN :KEY
  PRINT SENTENCE "down: :KEY
END

TO KEYUP :KEY
  PRINT SENTENCE "up: :KEY
END

TO CLICKDOWN :X :Y :BUTTON
  PENDOWN
END

TO CLICKUP :X :Y :BUTTON
  PENUP
END

ONKEY "keydown
ONKEYUP "keyup
ONCLICK "clickdown
ONRELEASE "clickup

PRINT 'Press/release keys or the mouse button on the canvas -- pen goes down on click, up on release.'
